From 7ceb7ab7c86f081cd6f88d3c48cec02333594971 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antigravity <antigravity@gemini.local>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 30/36] drm/amd/pm: Remove redundant mutex lock in SMU14 I2C
 update

smu_v14_0_2_i2c_xfer() takes adev->pm.mutex around the
smu_cmn_update_table() call. That lock is redundant: the SMU command
interface the call drives is already serialized by the SMU message
lock, and the I2C core serializes transfers on the adapter's own bus
lock. Worse, it is a self-deadlock hazard, because dpm entry points
such as amdgpu_dpm_force_performance_level() hold adev->pm.mutex and
can issue I2C transfers on this adapter, which would then block forever
on the nested acquisition.

Remove the mutex_lock()/mutex_unlock() pair around the table update.

Signed-off-by: Antigravity <antigravity@gemini.local>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu14/smu_v14_0_2_ppt.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu14/smu_v14_0_2_ppt.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu14/smu_v14_0_2_ppt.c
index e0ce16fb7..eed4fca09 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu14/smu_v14_0_2_ppt.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/swsmu/smu14/smu_v14_0_2_ppt.c
@@ -1962,9 +1962,7 @@ static int smu_v14_0_2_i2c_xfer(struct i2c_adapter *i2c_adap,
 			}
 		}
 	}
-	mutex_lock(&adev->pm.mutex);
 	r = smu_cmn_update_table(smu, SMU_TABLE_I2C_COMMANDS, 0, req, true);
-	mutex_unlock(&adev->pm.mutex);
 	if (r)
 		goto fail;
 
